<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / SYSTEM AUDIT</p>
    <h1>revdep</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Scan installed binaries and libraries for broken reverse dependencies.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># revdep [options]</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>revdep --help
revdep
revdep --check-file /usr/bin/example</code></pre>

    <p>
        Configure exclusions in <code>/etc/revdep.conf</code> and optional files
        under <code>/etc/revdep.d/*.conf</code>. The scan can inspect shared
        libraries and language modules; review exclusions carefully so a real
        broken dependency is not hidden.
    </p>
</section>
